 o:=$q$- [L2] TAG CHECK, VERSE SCOPE (pkgL2S rev 2; Citation Scan only): a word tag is bound to the verses of its own block. A line that opens with a bold MEANS or ANSWER (`**MEANS`, `**ANSWER`, any case, also after `>`, `-` or `_`; bold "Answer to [CR2] press" and bold "ANSWER CHECK" are such lines) starts a new block, so a tag under it binds to that block's verses and not to the whole LINK section, and a tag above it loses the verses below it. A MEANS or ANSWER line without bold, a bold MEANS in the middle of a line, and a markdown heading (`## ANSWER ...`, `# MEANS ...`) start no block. A tag under a bold ANSWER line takes that whole block, with no narrowing to its paragraph. The same block reader in the 20 other nodes (Extract, Build, L2 Count Plan) is unchanged, so the in-round checks keep the wider scope. Size: code +71, prompt 0. Limits: see section 17.$q$;
