- A "(Gn)" THAT POINTS TO A GRANT LABEL IN THE SAME ROUND IS NOT READ AS A STRONG'S NUMBER (pkgGLB, ASK 324; Shared Library tags() and countClaims(), LIB 158, 161, 201; 21 inline copies):
  - Why: the [L2] counter read grant pointers in a close ("granted at G17", "(G1, G7)", "(G47)") as Strong's numbers. In 37281 a tag read G1080, G5, gennaō, ek, where G5 was a grant label.
  - What it does: a G token is skipped in tags() and in countClaims()'s subject choice when both hold: (1) the same round holds a line that starts "G<n> [CR" or "G<n> [DR" (bold allowed) with that n; (2) the token is not in the citation form, which is an italic or starred transliteration, or Greek or Hebrew script, then an optional space, then "(" right before the G. A list continuation such as "(G21, G22)" is not the citation form. A number is kept if any of its uses in the segment is in the citation form. H tokens are never skipped. Helpers sit on LIB 158; tags() is LIB 161, countClaims() LIB 201.
  - Reach: the Shared Library (26 MAP users) and 21 inline copies change in step: Citation Scan, L2 Count Plan, C1/D2/C2/D3/C3/D4 Extract, C1B/D2B/C2B/D3B/C3B/D4B Extract, C3G Extract, and C2/C3/C4/D2/D3/D4 Build. Every node that holds "function tagWords(" is among them (W2 6802). PRS_LB needs no change (its derivation pattern needs 2 to 5 digits and voids no tag); Quote Report and the Lexicon Plans read numOf from rows only (W4 6801).
  - Size: Shared Library +817 on s217 (947,146 to 947,963); each inline copy +805, L2 Count Plan +842 (it has no countClaims).
  - Shown offline: tests 280 of 280 on 26 readers. 37281's tag goes from G1080, G5, gennaō, ek to G1080, gennaō, ek. "*abba* (G5)", "*abba*(G5)" and "ἀββα (G5)" with a G5 label stay counted; "(G5, G6)" with labels is skipped; G5 with no label and "(H5)" are kept; "granted at G5, 3 verses" after *ek* (G1537) now takes G1537. Replay over 60 debates, 8 columns: 9,537 tags, 29 changed, all in challenger_r4, all grant pointers; countClaims 34 claims, 0 changed. Hand check: 41 label-number tokens on [L2] lines, all grant pointers, 0 in citation form (W4 6801; W2 6802; W1 6803).
  - Limits: a transliteration written plain, without italics, beside a small Strong's number that is also a grant label ("abba (G5)" in a debate with a G5 grant) is skipped as a label; no case was measured, since the real numbers in the replay are far above the label range (W2 6802). a323/t.cjs and a324/t.cjs point at paths not in the repo (W1 6803). Code only, on the debater's own text; Ruling 383 is met. Live and UNEXERCISED.
  - WRITTEN AS s218 (ASK 324; n8n version ffc2f775).$q$);
 o:=$q$  - pkgCNV rev 3 (K-G4 retraction against the judge's own ANSWER CHECK): an ANSWER CHECK line with no C, D or G round label records nothing, and a reply that restates MEETS with no round label does not drop the record; a round written "[GR2]" is not read; a list that mixes rounds of both sides records the verse; a short book name, a verse range and a verse list are not matched to the line's verse; MISSES and MEETS on one verse for two presses records the verse; MEETS inside "CHANGE TO:" or in prose does not drop the record; a MISSES on the answer verse of the line records it. Not run from the raising check through to the cure check; no paid check.
  - pkgMUS rev 3 (ember, gemini and spark as alternates, reasoning effort low): one run seated ember: its reply carried its line breaks as escaped text, the line-anchored judge checks read no line, and its verdict entered the panel with only the single-verse and withdrawn-footing checks run; ember is out of the seat lists permanently (§10, EMBER REMOVED). No run has gone through since ember's entries were removed. No run has seated gemini or spark. Each model's fitness rests on one full-body check call at effort low. The follow-on calls to a seated alternate are read from the code, not run. The reserve path is open: the reserve is the first free alternate (hydrogen in the usual debate), and the database function odv1_record_panel_substitution holds a seat list that names no alternate seat, so a reserve substitution would be refused there; no run has reached it. Three more agreement calls per debate.
  - pkgHYD rev 2 (hydrogen as second alternate, reasoning effort low): no run has seated hydrogen. The model's fitness rests on one full-body check call at effort low. The follow-on calls to a seated hydrogen (send-back, gate, accept-return, question) are read from the code, not run. Nothing after the alternate step (the judgment rows of an alternate seat, the panel aggregate, the outcome) has run with hydrogen. One more agreement call per debate.$q$;
